Damage: 1d8+1 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 7
Proficiency Type: Axe
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 13 Strength

Weight: 7"

	SAY NAME2 "Stonefire +4"
	SAY DESC "The Stonefires were an old lineage of dwarves, and the eldest male of the line carried this axe, an heirloom of utmost importance. Unfortunately, they were decimated in 1150 DR, falling in a mere two years to a mysterious plague. Ulgan, keeper of the axe, fled in hopes of escaping the inevitable, but he died several weeks later. His body was found in the Cloakwood Forest, but the axe was missing.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +4 
Damage: 1d8+5, +1d4 fire damage
Damage type: slashing
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Axe
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 13 Strength

Weight: 7"




//AXE OF THE UNYIELDING +3 - 12000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/AX1H14.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Battle Axe"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The most common version of the battle axe is a stout pole about four feet in length with a single-edged, trumpet-shaped blade mounted on one end. This axe, in particular, appears to be very poorly made and slightly smaller than the average battle axe.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d8+1 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 7
Proficiency Type: Axe
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 13 Strength

Weight: 7"

	SAY NAME2 "Axe of the Unyielding +3"
	SAY DESC "The Axe of the Unyielding is a weapon born of stubbornness and iron will. Legend speaks of Glimred Heavyhand, an ancient dwarven defender who held alone a crumbling gate against an army of giants. When his shield shattered, he continued to fight with this axe, and it is said that his refusal to yield became a part of the metal itself. The blade is forged from a heavy, silver-grey alloy that never chips or dulls, regardless of how many necks it severs or how many spells it deflects. 

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities: 
- Immunity to Stun
– Armor Class: +2
– Saving Throws: +2

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d8+4 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 4
Proficiency Type: Axe
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 13 Strength

Weight: 7"


//AXE OF THE UNYIELDING +5 - 20000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/AX1H15.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Battle Axe"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The most common version of the battle axe is a stout pole about four feet in length with a single-edged, trumpet-shaped blade mounted on one end. This axe, in particular, appears to be very poorly made and slightly smaller than the average battle axe.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d8+1 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 7
Proficiency Type: Axe
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 13 Strength

Weight: 7"

	SAY NAME2 "Axe of the Unyielding +5"
	SAY DESC "The Axe of the Unyielding is a weapon born of stubbornness and iron will. Legend speaks of Glimred Heavyhand, an ancient dwarven defender who held alone a crumbling gate against an army of giants. When his shield shattered, he continued to fight with this axe, and it is said that his refusal to yield became a part of the metal itself. The blade is forged from a heavy, silver-grey alloy that never chips or dulls, regardless of how many necks it severs or how many spells it deflects. 
	
	Enhanced by the magic of the balor's claw, the Axe of the Unyielding is now the most fearsome of weapons — a vorpal-edged axe capable of severing an opponent's head with a single blow. 

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities: 
-Immunity to Stun
– Armor Class: +2
– Saving Throws: +2
- Magic Resistance: +10%

